{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I</b> — in gematria: כסא לו (His throne); for He rent all the firmaments to the Throne of Glory, and in gematria — מלא (full spelling) plus 10. And this is: 'Do I not fill heaven and earth?' (Jeremiah 23:24). And it contains ten Divine Names — first and last in heaven and on earth, and four directions, and depth and height." "<b>Who brought you out</b> — three times in the Masorah: אשר הוצאתיך / אשר הוצאתיך (in the Decalogue) / אשר הוצאתיך מאור כשדים — that He brought them out of Ur of the Chaldees to give His sons the Torah."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The phrase מלא ועוד עשרה likely means the gematria of אנכי equals the gematria of מלא (spelled מ״ם ל״מד א״לף, i.e. plene) plus 10; the expanded logic of the ten Ineffable Names is terse and left as is.", 1 "The three Masorah occurrences are cited without verse addresses; the first two are both from the Decalogue (Exodus 20:2 and Deuteronomy 5:6), the third from Genesis 15:7."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:46.353468984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}